    "text": "```python\nimport datetime\n\ndef parse_iso8601(s: str) -> datetime:\n    \"\"\"Parse an ISO-8601 timestamp string and return a timezone-aware datetime object.\"\"\"\n    # Check if the input is a naive timestamp (no offset or \"Z\")\n    if s.endswith(\"Z\"):\n        # Interpret as UTC\n        dt = datetime.datetime.strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n        return dt.replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)\n    elif \"+\" in s or \"-\" in s:\n        # Explicit offset\n        dt = datetime.datetime.strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S%z\")\n        return dt.replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone(dt.utcoffset()))\n    else:\n        # Naive timestamp (interpret as UTC)\n        dt = datetime.datetime.strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")\n        return dt.replace(tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)\n```\n# Examples:\n```python\n>>> parse_iso8601(\"2023-02-28T12:34:56Z\")\ndatetime.datetime(2023, 2, 28, 12, 34, 56, tzinfo=<UTC>)\n>>> parse_iso8601(\"2023-02-28T12:34:56+01:00\")\ndatetime.datetime(2023, 2, 28, 12, 34, 56, tzinfo=<UTC>)\n>>> parse_iso8601(\"2023-02-28T12:34:56-01:00\")\ndatetime.datetime(2023, 2, 28, 12, 34, 56, tzinfo=<UTC>)\n>>> parse_iso8601(\"2023-02-28T12:34:56\")\ndatetime.datetime(2023, 2, 28, 12, 34, 56, tzinfo=<UTC>)\n>>> parse_iso8601(\"invalid input\")\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\nValueError: Invalid ISO-8601 timestamp string\n```",
